1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:02,490
 As we said at the beginning, the four components that

2
00:00:02,490 --> 00:00:05,971
 we just saw can be connected by using intents. So,

3
00:00:05,971 --> 00:00:09,430
 what is an intent? An intent is an abstract description

4
00:00:09,430 --> 00:00:12,490
 of an operation to be performed and it consists of two

5
00:00:12,490 --> 00:00:15,730
 main parts, an action and a set of data. The

6
00:00:15,730 --> 00:00:18,740
 action is the action to be performed, which is indicated as

7
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:21,480
 a string. And the data is the data on which

8
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:25,920
 the action will operate. For example, consider a phone call intent.

9
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:28,930
 Such an intent might have call as an action.

10
00:00:28,930 --> 00:00:31,970
 And, information from the contact database, in particular

11
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:34,220
 a phone number, as data. So, why are

12
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:37,390
 intents useful? Well, because they provide the developers with

13
00:00:37,390 --> 00:00:41,020
 a way to perform late binding between different

14
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:44,770
 applications to connect applications that were not initially meant

15
00:00:44,770 --> 00:00:47,190
 to be connected. That is, they allow for

16
00:00:47,190 --> 00:00:51,790
 binding at run time to otherwise completely decoupled applications.

17
00:00:51,790 --> 00:00:54,210
 So let's see an example of how this works. To do

18
00:00:54,210 --> 00:00:57,510
 that, let's use the same example as before. So imagine that

19
00:00:57,510 --> 00:01:01,570
 you're browsing your contacts, so activity one will be the contact

20
00:01:01,570 --> 00:01:04,950
 application. So an activity in the contacts application. So you use that

21
00:01:04,950 --> 00:01:07,470
 activity and you get to the person that you want to

22
00:01:07,470 --> 00:01:11,000
 call. At this point you click on the phone icon and

23
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,310
 the result is the generation of an intent. And the intent

24
00:01:14,310 --> 00:01:16,890
 is exactly the one that we saw before. It's an intent in

25
00:01:16,890 --> 00:01:19,480
 which the action is call, and the data is the

26
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:22,300
 phone number for the person that you want to call. When

27
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:25,610
 this intent is generated what happens is that the call

28
00:01:25,610 --> 00:01:29,030
 activity of the phone app is being activated with the final

29
00:01:29,030 --> 00:01:32,090
 result that the person that you were looking up will

30
00:01:32,090 --> 00:01:35,500
 be called by your phone. So why does that happen? How

31
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:38,090
 can it be that I perform an action in one activity

32
00:01:38,090 --> 00:01:41,910
 and another activity is started as a consequence? To answer that,

33
00:01:41,910 --> 00:01:44,490
 let's see how the binding between these two activities

34
00:01:44,490 --> 00:01:47,470
 happens through intents. And there's different ways in which that

35
00:01:47,470 --> 00:01:51,250
 can happen. The first possibility is a direct binding.

36
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:54,641
 In this case the activity or the app generating the

37
00:01:54,641 --> 00:01:58,760
 intent will directly start an activity from another application.

38
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:01,450
 Similarly, the app generating the intent could directly start the

39
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:04,700
 service. For example, by requesting an audio player service

40
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:07,710
 to play a given audio file or a stream. Finally,

41
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:11,039
 and this is the most interesting type of binding,

42
00:02:11,039 --> 00:02:14,370
 the activity generating the intent, so in this case the

43
00:02:14,370 --> 00:02:18,200
 contacts application, could broadcast the event. And in this

44
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:21,570
 case the intent will be delivered to all interested broadcaster

45
00:02:21,570 --> 00:02:24,840
 receivers. So we just saw the broadcast receivers and

46
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:27,570
 this is the way in which some information can be

47
00:02:27,570 --> 00:02:30,194
 broadcasted. So in this case clearly it would not be

48
00:02:30,194 --> 00:02:32,850
 a system event but it will be an application event.

49
00:02:32,850 --> 00:02:34,820
 Going back to our example of the phone call,

50
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:38,870
 because the phone application previously notified the Android system

51
00:02:38,870 --> 00:02:41,410
 that it was supporting the action call, the system

52
00:02:41,410 --> 00:02:44,510
 will notify the phone app that a call intent has

53
00:02:44,510 --> 00:02:47,900
 been generated. So that's why this works. The phone

54
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:51,250
 app says, I can handle calls. When a call intent

55
00:02:51,250 --> 00:02:55,220
 is broadcasted, the activity is bound to the intent.

56
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:57,870
 The activity is notified about the intent, and can react

57
00:02:57,870 --> 00:03:00,330
 to it. And in case you're curious, this also the

58
00:03:00,330 --> 00:03:03,300
 reason why for instance if you have more than one app

59
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:05,490
 that can make phone calls, for example you have a voice

60
00:03:05,490 --> 00:03:08,490
 over IP application or multiple ones, and you have your regular

61
00:03:08,490 --> 00:03:12,420
 phone application, when you select the phone icon in your contacts

62
00:03:12,420 --> 00:03:15,390
 you are provided with a choice of which app to use

63
00:03:15,390 --> 00:03:19,230
 to call. That's because there are multiple parties, multiple activities, that

64
00:03:19,230 --> 00:03:23,055
 could handle that intent and therefore unless you define some default

65
00:03:23,055 --> 00:03:26,240
 behavior you will have to choose which one should be activated as

66
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:30,050
 a consequence of the generation of the intent. So, similar to broadcast

67
00:03:30,050 --> 00:03:35,000
 receivers, intents are also extremely useful in many situations to bind the

68
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,430
 activities that would be otherwise completely

69
00:03:37,430 --> 00:03:37,430
 decoupled, as we said at the beginning.

